course: dictionary
lesson: 12765
title: Earnestly: serious and sincere
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: "Earnestly" is an adverb. It tells you how someone does something. When someone does something earnestly, they are serious and sincere, so they really mean what they say or do. «Ben said earnestly, "I am sorry I broke your toy."» Ben is not joking. He really means it.
explain: "Earnestly" can also mean trying hard and with great care. «Maya worked earnestly on her project, checking every step twice.» Maya is not rushing or being careless. She is putting all her effort into it.
explain: Look for clue words that go with earnestly, such as said, promised, hoped or worked. Ask yourself: is this person being serious and sincere, or trying very hard? If yes, earnestly probably fits. Then swap in your meaning, such as "really meant it", and check that the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Earnestly means in a serious and sincere way, really meaning what you say or do.
fact: Earnestly can also mean trying hard and with great care.
fact: Earnestly is an adverb, so it tells you how something is done, often after a verb such as said, hoped or worked.
fact: «Earnestly» is similar to «sincerely» and «seriously» in its first meaning, and to «carefully» in its second.
fact: «She said earnestly, "I will keep my promise."» Here earnestly shows that she really means it.
exercise: «Lily earnestly promised to look after the puppy.» What does earnestly show? | She was joking and laughing | *She really meant it, in a serious and sincere way | She was too tired to talk | She had lost the puppy
exercise: «Tom worked earnestly on his model, measuring every piece twice.» What does earnestly mean here? | *Trying hard, with great care | Quickly and carelessly | Sleepily, in the corner | Loudly, so everyone could hear
exercise: «The old man earnestly hoped the rain would stop.» Find the word that tells you HOW he hoped. | stop | *earnestly | old | rain
test: «"I will keep my promise," Zara said earnestly.» Which meaning fits best? | She was being silly and playful | *She was being serious and sincere | She was lost in thought | She was fast asleep
test: Jayden says earnestly is just like seriously. Why might an author choose earnestly instead? | It means the same as silly, so it is a fun word | It is a noun for a kind of weather | *It shows the person is sincere and really means it | It is only used for numbers
exam: Which word means trying hard and with great care? | *earnestly | loudly | sleepily | sadly
